From b5cee6e30125957891e9493bfac9b944fd8ff4ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 14:47:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): carry admission-bound session models in run
 evidence [daveey]

A class-routed author run could terminate without worker_result, leaving only
selector evidence on the Board. Ship then could not establish independence.
Local state.db fallback repaired single-host runs but could not prove runs
spread across workers. The root gap was terminal evidence publication depending
on one best-effort process-exit event; tests covered only local recovery.

Stamp every terminal run event with concrete models read from the admitting
host's managed state.db. Require every admission, local origin, managed path
and in-run session start. Omit unknown evidence rather than guess. Add an
idempotent attest-run-models CLI for history, including evicted foreign copies;
append testimony without waking or altering closed tasks.

Proof: initial baseline had 15 expected regression failures. Forward and
historical regressions now pass including real continue/review/dependency,
CLI registration, dead-pid finalizer, and cross-Board replay. 34 model tests,
58 finalizer/reconciliation tests, 31 pickup/sync consumers pass. Full
scripts/check --base origin/main passes. Companion state gate verifies all
admission origins before using portable models; independent review and CI
remain mandatory. Task t_873214a6f9f5556f.
